<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Shizong of Jin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1123–<a href="/years/1189">1189</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Wanyan Yong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Shizong of Jin, Wanyan Yong, reigned over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a> from 1161 to 1189 after the overthrow of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wanyan-liang">Prince Hailing</a>. He made peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Southern Song</a> in 1165 and promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> language and traditions while Confucian learning flourished. His long, stable reign is regarded as the high point of the dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-shizong-of-jin.jpg" alt="Emperor Shizong of Jin" width="297" height="492" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 陳世倌 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%81%96%E5%B8%9D%E6%98%8E%E7%8E%8B%E5%96%84%E7%AB%AF%E9%8C%84%EF%BC%88%E5%AE%8B%E5%85%83%E6%98%8E%EF%BC%89_%E5%86%8A_%E9%87%91%E4%B8%96%E5%AE%97_K2A003132N000000011PAB_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Emperor Shizong</b> (r. 1161–1189), remembered by Chinese historians as a model ruler, made peace with the Song in 1165, reformed taxation and worried that the Jurchen were losing their identity: he promoted the Jurchen language, had Chinese classics translated into it and created examinations in Jurchen in 1173.</blockquote><a href="/empire/jin-dynasty-1115-1234">Jin dynasty (1115-1234) · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huining-prefecture">Huining</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=45.5,126.97&amp;year=1165" aria-label="Huining on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7562 559 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Emperor Shizong of Jin"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8012 829h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8012 829h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=45.5,126.97&amp;year=1165">What was here in 1165? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
